From 6bed91186903d833c7c6653a155dea9910d71794 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: John Stringer <jcec_1@yahoo.co.uk>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 07:40:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 04/37] Speed-up E: inline Z80 data memory access, run-based
 CRTC stepping

The CRTC is stepped in runs up to its next event instead of one character at
a time, and Z80 data reads/writes through the memory map are inlined.
Pixel-exact on the test set; NO_E restores the per-step loop.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
